{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.JetTowerBlindToDecay","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.JetTowerBlindToDecay","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.decay_combination_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.decay_combination_zero","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/JetTowerBlindToDecay.lean#L83-L90","doc":"The decay combination therefore vanishes identically at every level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.sum_eq_of_involution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.sum_eq_of_involution","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/JetTowerBlindToDecay.lean#L62-L81","doc":"**The reindexing that makes the tower blind to decay.** On a finite index set\nclosed under an involution `t`, if the weight `W` is `t`-invariant and the two\nmultiplicities swap under `t`, the two weighted sums coincide — so their\n*difference*, which is what the decay channel sees, vanishes identically.\n\nInstantiated at `ι =` partitions of `k`, `t =` transpose, `W =` the q-Plancherel\nweight (a function of the hook multiset, which transpose permutes) and\n`m₁, m₂ =` the trivial and sign branching multiplicities. ","signatureChunk":0}]}